@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/proposal#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "NoteProof: Bitcoin timestamps and an AI-tagged knowledge graph for students' lecture notes"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "Give every Note author a way to register a lecture note and receive a proof, anchored on the Bitcoin signet in the way Nakamoto's timestamp server describes, that the note existed in their hands on that day; let an AI tagger file each note under a shared course and topic vocabulary; and let every Note reader find notes by topic, see who registered each one first, and be warned about copies of earlier notes." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "A student uploads a note after class, confirms the course and topics the AI suggests, and the next day holds a proof linked to a Bitcoin transaction; before the exam a classmate searches a topic, finds that note with its author and date, and anyone can check the proof without trusting the archive or the people who run it." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:Customer1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "3rd- and 4th-year Software Engineering students at İstanbul Kültür University"@en ; rdfs:comment "Customer (owner): one archive where their notes are found by course and topic, credited to the students who registered them, with a proof anyone can check"@en .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Note author"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: students who write their own lecture notes and share them with classmates - uploads a note, confirms its course and topics, and receives a timestamp proof (weekly, phone or laptop browser)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Note reader"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: students who look for notes before quizzes and exams - searches notes by course and topic and checks who registered each note first (weekly, phone)"@en .
ex:EndUser3 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Note verifier"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: a classmate, a lecturer or a club jury settling who had a note first - opens a note's proof page and checks when and by whom it was registered (occasional, laptop browser)"@en .
