ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Every note is tagged with a course and topics from the shared vocabulary"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "an untagged note cannot be found" .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Readers find notes by topic and are warned about copies of earlier notes"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "search and the copy warning are what readers use" .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "No note content or personal data reaches the chain, and no AI tag is saved without the author's confirmation"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "KVKK forbids the first; trust in the archive forbids the second" .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The system lets a student upload a lecture note as a PDF, a photo or text. It computes the note's SHA-256 hash and records the registration with PROV-O. An AI tagger reads the note's text and suggests a course, topics from the SKOS vocabulary and a two-sentence summary; nothing is saved until the author confirms, and the SHACL shapes refuse a note without a course or with an unknown topic. A copy check compares the new note with earlier notes and links possible copies to the earlier note's proof. Once a day the timestamp service builds a Merkle tree of the day's hashes and writes its root in an OP_RETURN output of a Bitcoin signet transaction, giving each note a Merkle path. Readers search by course and topic, including narrower topics. A public proof page recomputes a note's hash, walks its Merkle path and shows the block time, without needing the archive's server." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a note registered and confirmed today, when the daily timestamp has one confirmation, then the note's proof page shows its hash, its Merkle path, the signet txid and the block time" .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a note file that was changed by one character after it was timestamped, when its proof is checked, then the hash does not match and the page says it is not the registered file" .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a note whose author picks a topic that is not in the vocabulary, when the author confirms it, then the note is refused and the author is asked to choose a topic from the list" .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Notes with a valid timestamp proof within 24 hours"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of pilot notes whose Merkle path verifies against a confirmed signet transaction within 24 hours of upload, %" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Notes tagged with a valid course and topics"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of pilot notes whose confirmed tags pass the shapes, %" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "100" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "AI topic suggestions accepted unchanged"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Judged ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of suggested topics that authors confirm without correction on the 60 evaluation notes, %" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "80" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Minutes to find a note on a topic before an exam"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "median minutes a student needs to find a note on one topic: now, the middle of the survey's median answer (10 to 20 minutes, 20 students); in the pilot, timed for 20 searches" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "15" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "2" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O5 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Planted copies caught by the copy warning"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "share of the 20 planted copies in the evaluation set that the copy warning flags, %" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "90" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O6 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Note content, personal data or unconfirmed tags leaked"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "OP_RETURN outputs holding anything but a 32-byte root, plus saved tags the author did not confirm" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Swimlanes: Note author · NoteProof services · Bitcoin signet · Note reader or verifier\n\nA. Register a note\n1. Start: the note author uploads a note (PDF, photo or text).\n2. The registration service checks the file type and size. [not allowed] → the upload is refused with the reason → end.\n3. It computes the note's SHA-256 hash. [hash already registered] → the page shows the earlier registration and its proof → end.\n4. Fork, in parallel:\n   4a. The AI tagger extracts the text and suggests a course, topics from the SKOS vocabulary and a two-sentence summary.\n   4b. The copy checker compares the text with earlier notes.\n5. Join: the author sees the suggestions and any similar earlier note.\n6. The author confirms or corrects every tag. [author cancels] → nothing is saved → end.\n7. pySHACL validates the confirmed tags against the shapes. [invalid] → the violations are shown and the author returns to step 6.\n8. [similar earlier note found] → the note is marked as a possible copy and linked to the earlier note's proof.\n9. The note and its PROV-O registration are stored and its hash is queued; the author sees \"proof pending\". End of the author's flow.\n\nB. Daily timestamp (time event: every day at 23:00)\n10. The timestamp service collects the day's queued hashes. [queue empty] → end.\n11. It builds the Merkle tree and puts the 32-byte root in an OP_RETURN output.\n12. It broadcasts the transaction to the Bitcoin signet through Bitcoin Core and waits for one confirmation. [not confirmed within 6 blocks] → it bumps the fee and broadcasts again.\n13. It stores the txid, the block height and each note's Merkle path, and marks the notes \"timestamped\". End.\n\nC. Find and check a note\n14. The reader searches by course and topic; the search also covers narrower topics.\n15. The reader opens a note card with its author, date and proof badge.\n16. On the proof page the browser recomputes the file's hash, walks its Merkle path and fetches the block from a public signet node.\n17. [hash and root match] → \"proven\", with the block time. [no match] → \"not the registered file\". End." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "The upload page sends the file to the registration service, which computes the SHA-256 hash, extracts the text and asks the tagger and the copy checker in parallel. The tagger asks the language model for concepts limited to the SKOS vocabulary and returns them; the copy checker compares the text's embedding with earlier notes and returns any match. The author confirms; the service asks pySHACL to validate and stores the note and its PROV-O registration in Oxigraph. Each night the timestamp service reads the day's hashes, builds the Merkle tree, asks the Bitcoin Core signet node to fund and broadcast an OP_RETURN transaction, waits for a confirmation and stores the txid and each Merkle path. The proof page recomputes the hash in the browser, walks the path and asks a public signet node for the block." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Note is a schema:CreativeWork identified by its SHA-256 hash, with a title, a file type, a summary, one Course and one or more Topics. Course and Topic are skos:Concepts in one scheme, linked by skos:broader and skos:narrower. Registration is a prov:Activity that generated the Note's record, associated with a StudentAccount (pseudonymous) at a time. A new version of a note is a new Note linked by prov:wasRevisionOf. DailyTimestamp holds a date, a Merkle root, a signet txid and a block height; every Note has one Proof, its Merkle path, pointing to a DailyTimestamp. CopyWarning links a Note to an earlier Note with a similarity score." .
